-- title:
--   Test functions cutting out the residue tube of a supersingular place
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, and write $\kappa$ for its residue field and $\mathfrak m_A$ for its maximal ideal. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'=\kappa(\,\mathrm{jqModC}\,\kappa,\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\kappa\,M')\subseteq\kappa((t))$ (a place being a proper valuation subring containing $\kappa$ whose ideals are principal) consisting exactly of the elements of $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'\,\kappa$, i.e. of those $w$ that are rational over $\kappa$, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace` and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M')\in\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\kappa$. Let $F=\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, assume $F\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'=:F'$, the corresponding base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, and let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $F$ along $A$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ (a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ together with a surjective residue map onto the target with kernel its maximal ideal, a compatible map on places preserving degrees and orders, and the compatibility with $A$), assumed to be the coefficientwise reduction: every Laurent series over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in $F$ is $R_0$-integral with $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction along $A\to\kappa$. Then for each $s\in W$ there are $k\in\mathbb N$ and $w_1,\dots,w_k\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that: each $w_j$ has nonnegative order at every place of $F/\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the coefficientwise image of $j_q$ has nonnegative order, its residue $\overline{w_j}$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\overline{w_j})$ is the residue of $0$; and, for every rational place $P$ of $F'/\overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that all the $w_j$, viewed in $F'$, lie in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(w_j)\in\mathfrak m_A$, one has: for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose order is nonnegative wherever that of the coefficientwise image of $j_q$ is, whose residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $a\in A$ with residue $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,f)$, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)-a$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$.
--
--   This is the construction of a finite family of test functions on the level-$M'$ modular function field that cuts out the residue tube (formal fibre) of a supersingular place $s$ of the reduction: simultaneous smallness of the $w_j$ at a rational place $P$ of the full-level curve forces $P$ to specialise to $s$ on all functions regular away from the cusps. It feeds the Type II exhaustion arguments [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.typeII_exhaustion_of_placeCover_of_componentChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.typeII_exhaustion_of_placeCover_of_componentChart) and its two variants.
